<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Kalala Ilunga</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">r. c. 1585</span> · <a href="/centuries/16th-century">16th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Kalala Ilunga is the figure credited in oral tradition with founding the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/second-luba-dynasty">Second Luba Dynasty</a> around 1585. He defeated and executed his predecessor <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nkongolo-mwamba">Nkongolo Mwamba</a> and consolidated chiefdoms under a new <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sacred-kingship">sacred kingship</a>. He is regarded as the architect of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/luba-empire">Luba Empire</a>.</p></div>
